**`apps/web/src/dungeon/fight/FightScreen.test.tsx`**, in `describe("R4852000 a fight a Glitch voided is dealt again, never reported", …)`:
- `it("R4852000 a voided fight asks for no report, offers no Continue, and Deal it again deals the same fight fresh from its seed")`:
  - Set up `fightHost([], false, "failed", 0, {}, { winner: "draw", reason: "voided" })` with `act` and `holdReport` mocks, via `fakeDungeon(act, 65_000, holdReport)`.
  - After `concedeOnBoard()`, `await screen.findByTestId(fightTestid.voided)` has the text "A Glitch voided this fight".
  - `fightTestid.continue` and `fightTestid.reportError` are absent, and `host.reports()` is 0.
  - Click `fightTestid.redeal`, then `await waitFor(() => expect(host.starts()).toHaveLength(2))`.
  - `host.starts()[1]` equals `expect.objectContaining({ seed: SETUP.seed, humanSeat: "p1", run: SETUP })`, and `host.resumes()` stays 1.
  - `await waitFor(() => expect(screen.queryByTestId(fightTestid.voided)).toBeNull())`.
  - `act` and `holdReport` are never called.
- `it("R4852000 Menu after a void goes to Play and sends the run nothing")`:
  - Call `at(paths.dungeon)` and use the same host.
  - After the void note shows, click `fightTestid.resultMenu`.
  - `window.location.pathname` is `paths.play`, and there is no `leaveDialog`.
  - After `cleanup()`, `act` has not been called; then `at("/")`.

